  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "What is the value of\n\n\\[ \\begin{aligned} &(\\log 5)^3+(\\log 20)^3 \\\\ &\\quad {}+(\\log 8)(\\log 0.25) \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nwhere \\(\\log\\) denotes the base-ten logarithm?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac32\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac74\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac94\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(3\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2022-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(u=\\log 2.\\) Then \\(\\log 5=1-u,\\) \\(\\log 20=1+u,\\) \\(\\log 8=3u,\\) and \\(\\log 0.25=-2u.\\)\n\nWith \\(a=1-u,\\ b=1+u,\\) we have \\(a+b=2\\) and \\(ab=1-u^2,\\) so \\[ \\begin{gathered} a^3+b^3 \\\\ =(a+b)\\big((a+b)^2-3ab\\big) \\\\ =2\\big(4-3(1-u^2)\\big) \\\\ =2+6u^2. \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nThe last term is \\((3u)(-2u)=-6u^2,\\) so the total is \\(2+6u^2-6u^2=2.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Let \\(u=\\log 2;\\) then \\(\\log 5=1-u\\) and \\(\\log 20=1+u\\)",
        "Also \\(\\log 8=3u\\) and \\(\\log 0.25=-2u;\\) use \\(a^3+b^3=(a+b)(a^2-ab+b^2)\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
